<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Further plots</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix F Further plots ‣ Influence Functions for Efficient Data Selection in Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> visualizes how our pruning strategy outperforms other baselines for Llama3-8B-Instruct, while results are inconclusive on cross-family transfer with Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06108v1/pruning_bars_llama10_delta_random.svg" id="A6.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/279;" width="476" height="279"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A6.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLaMA-3-8B-Instruct</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06108v1/pruning_bars_qwen10_delta_random.svg" id="A6.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/279;" width="476" height="279"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A6.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A6.F4.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<math id="A6.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.F4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pass@1 vs. Random pruning on benchmarks.</span>
<em id="A6.F4.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em> For LLaMA-3-8B-Instruct, our IF-based Combined pruning achieves larger gains than baselines, particularly on GSM8k and OlympiadBench. On GPQA, <em id="A6.F4.9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Combined</em> mitigates this degradation more effectively than other pruning strategies.
<em id="A6.F4.9.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em> For Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct ( 10% pruning), improvements do not transfer reliably: all methods remain close to <em id="A6.F4.9.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Random</em>, with AMC23 showing inconsistent deviations.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
